<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28738" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mentor</span></b> , ŏris,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέντωρ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The famous friend of Odysseus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 9,
				8, 2</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A celebrated artist in embossed work in metal</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 18, § 38</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				33, 12, 53, § 147</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> transf., <i>a
			Mentor-cup</i>, a skilfully wrought drinking-vessel: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rarae sine Mentore mensae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 104</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mentora frangere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 11, 5</span></i>
			.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mentŏrĕus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Mentor the artist, Mentorean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 14, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">labores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 39, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
